    <DataNode elementId="AT1G79870-MONOMER" textLabel="Glyoxylate/hydroxypyruvate reductase A HPR2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9CA90" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="275" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Three isoforms of glycerate dehydrogenase/hydroxypyruvate reductases (HPRs) are present in the peroxisomes (|FRAME: AT1G68010 HPR1|) |CITS: [9177031]|, the cytosol (|FRAME: AT1G79870 HPR2|) |CITS: [3548703][3281657][16667010][2039466][18952776]|, and also in plastids (|FRAME: AT1G12550 HPR3|) |CITS: [16666441][21205613]|. The cytosolic |FRAME: AT1G79870 HPR2| preferentially uses NADPH over NADH |CITS: [3281657][16653027]|. In contrast to |FRAME: AT1G68010 HPR1|, |FRAME: AT1G79870 HPR2| is inhibited by oxalate, tartronate and phosphohydroxypyruvate |CITS: [16667783][2039466][21205613]|. It is also inhibited by supraoptimal concentrations of |FRAME: OH-PYR hydroxypyruvate| |CITS: [3281657][16653027]|, which may be important in regulation of serine biosynthesis when photorespiration is active. The pool of cytosolic |FRAME: GLYCERATE (&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-glycerate| used by |FRAME: AT1G79870 HPR2| may also serve as substrate for a cytosolic isozyme of |FRAME: EC-2.7.1.31 EC 2.7.1.31, glycerate 3-kinase| |CITS: [ 29129375]|. The combined activity of the two enzymes constitutes a cytoplasmic bypass of photorespiration, as the product |FRAME: G3P 3-phospho-D-glycerate| will enter glycolysis in the cytosol rather than the Calvin cycle in the chloroplasts.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G79870-MONOMER" />
