    <DataNode elementId="AT1G12550-MONOMER" textLabel="Glyoxylate/hydroxypyruvate reductase HPR3" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9LE33" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="355" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Three isoforms of glycerate dehydrogenase/hydroxypyruvate reductases (HPRs) are present in the peroxisomes (|FRAME: AT1G68010 HPR1|) |CITS: [9177031]|, the cytosol (|FRAME: AT1G79870 HPR2|) |CITS: [3548703][3281657][16667010][2039466][18952776]|, and also in plastids (|FRAME: AT1G12550 HPR3|) |CITS: [16666441][21205613]|. A minor HPR activity (up to 10%) associated with the chloroplast fraction of pea protoplasts was reported already in 1988 |CITS: [16666441]|. However, the enzyme was identified only in 2011 from Arabidopsis |CITS: [21205613]|. The deletion of |FRAME: AT1G12550 HPR3| by T-DNA insertion mutagenesis results in slightly altered leaf concentrations of the photorespiratory intermediates |FRAME: OH-PYR hydroxypyruvate|, |FRAME: GLYCERATE (&lt;i&gt;R&lt;/i&gt;)-glycerate|, and |FRAME: GLY glycine|, indicating a disrupted photorespiratory flux, but not in visible alteration of the phenotype. However a triple mutant in |FRAME: AT1G68010 HPR1|, |FRAME: AT1G79870 HPR2|, and |FRAME: AT1G12550 HPR3| does show increased growth retardation, decreased photochemical efficiency, and reduced oxygen-dependent gas exchange compared with an |FRAME: AT1G68010 HPR1|/|FRAME: AT1G79870 HPR2| double mutant. |FRAME: AT1G12550 HPR3| is active with |FRAME: OH-PYR hydroxypyruvate| and even more with |FRAME: GLYOX glyoxylate|, and is located in the cholroplasts |CITS: [21205613]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G12550-MONOMER" />
